            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="0706" n="604" xml:id="pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.24/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Newson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-22T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 22—9:34
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Colt agent, Warsaw is attempting to secure orders for 600 aircraft machine
                    guns from Polish war office and asks Legation’s immediate assistance.</p>
                <p>Am informed strong pressure being brought in favor of Vickers by British Legation
                    here and French military mission supporting Hotchkiss.</p>
                <p>Does the Department desire Legation to take action similar to that instructed in
                    Department’s telegram 70, August 6, 3 p.m., 1925?</p>
                <p>Please instruct by telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Newson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
